{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>For not like our Rock is their Rock.</b> And furthermore: for they knew and saw that their Rock is not like our Rock — for all the while that Israel do the will of the Omnipresent, neither they nor their Rock have power over Israel, for on the contrary, the Holy One, blessed be He, executed judgments upon them and upon their gods. And also upon Dagon, because of the Ark, as it is said: ״כי כבדה ידו עלינו ועל דגון אלהינו״. And now our enemies are judges over us, judging us as they wish. Another interpretation: ״כי לא כצורנו צורם״ — and our enemies did not become judges over our Rock, after they had become judges over their rock; and after they do not know to set their minds to all this — I fear lest they anger Me by this, that they attribute all dominion to themselves. They should have understood that since Israel, who are the children of the Omnipresent, were punished for the wickedness of their deeds, all the more so should they [the enemies] fear for themselves by a fortiori reasoning. And now it goes on to explain ״מה אחריתם״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The word פלילים, which appears multiple times, carries the sense of 'judges/adversaries who impose judgment'; rendered consistently as 'judges' to preserve the repetition. The idiom לישא ק\"ו rendered as 'to fear by a fortiori reasoning,' reading לישא as bearing/fearing the kal vachomer inference."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:57.195336572Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}